Code blocks of Texy 3
=====================

A block named after its language:

/--php
$texy = new Texy\Texy;
echo $texy->toHtml($text);
\--

The language written as a parameter of /--code, with a modifier:

/--code js .[example]
	if (ok) {
		alert('Hello');
	}
\--

- install the package

  /--bash
  composer require texy/texy
  \--

- and you are done

> A quote can hold code as well:
>
> /--neon
> texy:
>     headingLevel: 2
> \--

These stay as they are:

```php
echo 'already a fence';
```

/--html
<b>a built-in type</b>
\--

/--foo bar
a type that is not a language name
\--
